@* The section's tabs: the population first, then the comparison drawn from it, then the KINDS of test
   that are declared but not built.

   Runs is every run this store holds — reading, fix and tool-lane alike — and Arms is the comparison
   over whatever axis those runs varied: a compute backend, a tool lane, a retrieval variant, a fix arm.
   The tab used to be named "Sidecar" after the first axis anyone compared, and the label outlived the
   truth: measured on a real reader 2026-08-21, the operator asked why an investigate run showed under a
   hardware tab. The old routes survive on the pages as bookmark aliases.

   RAG and MCP stay declared before they are built, deliberately: the structure is the claim about what
   this section is for, and a tab that appears later reads as a feature nobody planned. Each says what
   will live there rather than rendering an empty page. *@

